 "query": "I swung by the community garden on my walk over here this morning, and the tomato plants that the teen group put in back in May are finally heavy with fat, sun-warmed cherry tomatoes that pop with sweet juice the second you bite into them. One of the regulars who tends the herb bed passed around little paper cups of fresh lemon balm iced tea she\u2019d brewed at home, and it was so bright and minty I stayed to chat for 20 minutes instead of heading straight to my errand like I planned. A tiny calico cat that\u2019s been napping on the garden fence all summer curled up in my lap the whole time we talked, purring so loud I could feel it through my jeans even when a group of kids ran past chasing a stray butterfly. Right now I\u2019m browsing the men\u2019s mules & clogs section, and I\u2019ve heard pairs made with ethylene vinyl fit right in with that fun bold option I always gravitate toward for casual wear, and I\u2019ve heard none of those pairs go over my budget cap.",
